{"name":"Poolside","hex":"#bee0e2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poolside","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["By the side of a pool."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Beside a pool."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poolside"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poolside (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Poolside is an American nu-disco and chillwave band from Los Angeles, California, formed in 2011 by Jeffrey Paradise and Filip Nikolic. The band currently consists of Jeffrey Paradise with additional touring members of Vito Roccoforte, Mattie Safer, Alton Allen, and Casey Butler (Pharaohs)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Poolside_ReithHumphreys_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Poolside_ReithHumphreys_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poolside_(band)"},{"title":"Poolside (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Poolside is the third studio album by the American pop–Latin freestyle–electronic dance music duo Nu Shooz. It was released on May 9, 1986, through Atlantic Recording Corporation. Recording sessions took place at Sunset Sound Factory and Lorber Studio in Los Angeles, Atlantic Studios in New York, Cascade Recording and Spectrum Studios in Portland. Production was handled by John Smith and Rick Waritz, with Jeff Lorber, Marlon McClain and Shep Pettibone serving as associate producers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/Nushooz_poolside1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poolside_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/OUTSIDELANDS2023_0813_161507-4734_ALIVECOVERAGE-1536x1025.jpg/500px-OUTSIDELANDS2023_0813_161507-4734_ALIVECOVERAGE-1536x1025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/